/E (A 99-minute program of modernist experimental masterpieces, including A Colour Box \(dir. Len Lye, 1935, 3 min\), Trade Tattoo \(dir. Len Lye, 1937, 3 min\), Night Mail \(dir. Basil Wright and Harry Watt, 1936, 30min\) and Borderline \(dir. Kenneth Macpherson, 1930, 63 min\) at the ODEON Theatre, Loughborough. Followed by a post-screening reception at Jam Garden, also generously funded by Texas A&M University. Tickets for the screening are limited. All are welcome to the reception from 9pm. )
