/E (The MSA Film Studies SIG presents a curated series of films, running alongside the official conference programme. Bringing modernist masterpieces from around the world to Loughborough, the series will showcase experimental shorts, documentaries, archival titles, and feature films over three days of the BAMS/MSA conference. Free to attend for all delegates, this has been made possible due to the generous support of the Visual, Material and Performance Cultures section and the College of Performance, Visualization & Fine Arts at Texas A&M University. Led by Jordan Brower, John Hoffmann, and Aurore Spiers, this collaborative undertaking will complement and extend the conference themes, each introduced by invited experts:  )
